  "structure": {
    "block_count": 49,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Searching for a Dashing Baby Boy Name? These 15 British Boy Names Deliver",
        "text_sha256": "7c823702a27628aed020df6ec3c5530856ac16c7726fb28cbbc816b888bc7536",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Updates to copy, sources, and formatting.",
        "text_sha256": "2bf448333081ffc8549a45a6c4b7fc711ee4b93575f0fffd3c4a6212c13581c2",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "british boy names",
        "text_sha256": "651185df2ce84af00907657c468e1ddf5fb8af8dfe7dd33a567c35280463afd6",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "From Alfie to Wylie, you'll love these short, sweet and punchy British names for your baby boy.",
        "text_sha256": "44c24ea1daeaecbe5ca020b8b683245a595d36567d36bc1fb07c03892a98dd68",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Wondering if a British name is for you? If you prefer a shorter name, then you might want to check out this list of British boy names for one- and two-syllable options. Or perhaps you happen to love names that are sweet and punchy in a really adorable way — then, one of these baby boy names from England, Scotland and Wales might just be a perfect fit.",
        "text_sha256": "3883f3e92949d33fc898c0b7d11f9df5b35f32a8d38e544dfa17159030f43fe2",
        "word_count": 68
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Want more British-inspired names for your baby-to-be? We’ve got brilliant options in the What to Expect app that are sure to suit your wee one.",
        "text_sha256": "7163fc02fa96aa883484fdbec5acb266f99b286c6332c6c89469da90659a8456",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Adney. It's different but not too out there; in fact, it's pretty close to the more popular Andy. This English name means \"noble's island.\"",
        "text_sha256": "cbb9cf94125755b1a81b3b05f0a0d48d99bf339443cad080102fdbc11536f5ee",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Alfie. Such a cute name for a little boy. It's a familiar form of the English name Alfred, meaning \"wise counselor.\"",
        "text_sha256": "33c91d61ff11c62c45c1f2a8cb908e95834f1a05038d68239fb988c228557c64",
        "word_count": 21
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Beck. If you're into one-syllable names, this is a winner. It means \"brook\" in the English tradition.",
        "text_sha256": "7ae87f3b887a065a8bd79faf15d6767179b9507ab0e47d594bbb34ca7d9fa753",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Bowen. Owen is a super popular name these days — and here's a slightly different twist. It's a Welsh name that means \"son of Owen.\"",
        "text_sha256": "a16aace97ff3ed4242b721018d6beb6526f16c5dc4a3dbaca089902340c00626",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Chance. If you suspect your son will be a bold and brave adventurer who isn't afraid to live life on his own terms, then consider this stunner. It's a familiar form of the English name Chancellor, which means \"record keeper.\"",
        "text_sha256": "995065bedfffd3e321cb40c46da86bc48aa9183320b5a891391b2153ef4eae7a",
        "word_count": 40
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Dougal. This Scottish name means \"dark stranger,\" and may give your son a hint of mystery.",
        "text_sha256": "2edbc62ada762ed9391c1321df13b9a03b88df92a993962b8707e2ad644b0c81",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Eddie. Is Edgar or Edward a family name? Then you might be drawn to this sweet, less formal alternative, which means \"prosperous guardian.\"",
        "text_sha256": "216754f3c6bfac712e4ad5eee386c408132e840d0cda2686c63fcee7ab27a3e5",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Graham. Another masculine-sounding name that's short and sweet. It means \"gray home\" in the English tradition. You might also consider the Scottish spelling: Graeme.",
        "text_sha256": "fb942287fcc17360af8ee88c5198ad3984bff80628984de5cd0b3ba0aa8ea750",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Hamilton. How about this classic name — which means \"proud estate\" in the English tradition — for your baby boy? Tony or Ham would make cute and unexpected nicknames.",
        "text_sha256": "0e940ccadb88d894ae371dbdf38e5a310e1db331027c5f0cf3ddcd3bd2b9be05",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Jestin. Like the name Justin (which is a Latin name meaning \"just\")? So do a lot of people. Consider this Welsh version to make your son stand out from the crowd.",
        "text_sha256": "cbd1bd51a6af6df6a9b4790eab17a8d77373b06df892529d8da50d3a71bcb7a0",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Kai. A great name to pair with a long last name. It's Welsh and means \"keeper of the keys.\"",
        "text_sha256": "ea638ef2828b15e3b357d172524937d4677fe3cd07c2c96b48fcf51489930795",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Ned. Here's another English familiar form of Edward. Plus, it's vintage-sounding, which might be perfect for your sweet baby boy.",
        "text_sha256": "72898086d0eb0c3b618de034faf579ab74abf0e3c40a20ab98767d9294c51564",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Smith. Yes, Smith is one of the most common last names of all time. But how often is it used as a first name? It means \"blacksmith\" in the English tradition.",
        "text_sha256": "fc448adc9118b2ddf51770f442425ce797f851c068b3b24a3b2e34f086355b59",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Tristan. If this name sounds like royalty to you, that's because there's a knight in the Arthurian legends named Tristan. It's Welsh and means \"noise” or “tumult.”",
        "text_sha256": "fe486829ecf86cdb8f11c359f588696c81195647b2ded3c7627931c69c00dcfb",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Wylie. This is a very cool-sounding name, and it suggests that its bearer may be quite clever. It means \"willow meadow.\"",
        "text_sha256": "26c92be103ad29a4852a64ec82880b5272a7cda0b64320069104ea28ed907df1",
        "word_count": 21
      },
      {
